GPU: sleep times that cannot be nanoseconds, a buffer closed twice, a fence never issued (HackiOS 7822f30).

Three faults in the RedwoodGPU service from values the caller chooses. A wait's seconds times
NSEC_PER_SEC overflowed, so a huge timeout became a past one (or a negative one); it is worked out
with __builtin_mul_overflow/__builtin_add_overflow now. freeBuffer() lets go of gGPULock while
gpuWait() waits, so a second close of the same handle could free its memory and GPU address twice:
the handle is emptied first and the work is done on a copy. And a wait for a fence that was never
issued waited until gpuWait() declared the GPU dead for every client; such a fence is refused with
kIOReturnBadArgument. The submission log no longer prints addresses[0]/words[0] when no command
buffer was among the commands. HackiOS's show() size check does not apply: this port's show() is
kIOReturnUnsupported (render tests read back).

